---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Profile from '../../layouts/Profile.astro';
import { person, site } from '../../data/site';
import { certification } from '../../data/software';
import portrait from '../../assets/photos/portrait-software.jpg';
---

<Profile
  path="software"
  title={`About · ${person.fullName}, Frontend & Full Stack Developer`}
  description={`About ${person.fullName}: a self-taught frontend and full stack developer from Port Harcourt, Nigeria, who learned through W3Schools and Frontend Mentor and now builds production web applications on contract.`}
>
  <div class="wrap about">
    <header class="about-head">
      <p class="label">~/software/about</p>
      <h1>I learned to build for the web by building for the web.</h1>
    </header>

    <figure class="about-photo">
      <Picture
        src={portrait}
        alt={`Portrait of ${person.fullName} in a light blue knit sweater`}
        widths={[320, 520, 760]}
        sizes="(min-width: 56rem) 30vw, 80vw"
        formats={['avif', 'webp']}
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="prose about-text">
      <p class="lead">
        I’m {person.fullName}, a frontend and full stack developer in Port Harcourt, Nigeria. I’m self-taught. I
        started in 2020 with W3Schools and have been building things ever since.
      </p>
      <p>
        Frontend Mentor became my training ground. Each challenge hands you a finished design and nothing else, so I
        had to work out layout, responsive behaviour and state on my own, then publish the result for other developers
        to review. That is where my habit of comparing what I built against the design, pixel by pixel, comes from.
      </p>
      <p>
        In 2022 I started Vortex Horizon, a small studio for websites and 3D model showcases, and built its site from
        scratch. Since then the work has moved further back into the stack. On my most recent contract, for JOPAD
        Advisory, I wrote the Node.js and Express API, designed the MongoDB data, connected Google Calendar, Resend and
        Airtable, and ran the production deployment across Vercel and Render. On another contract, a fundraising site
        called Jason, I used React and TypeScript.
      </p>

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>I put the rules that matter on the server, not just in the browser, which is why JOPAD checks every booking slot on the server.</li>
        <li>I treat the unglamorous parts as part of the job: transactional emails, spam protection, analytics, sitemaps and environment configuration.</li>
        <li>I match the tools to the project rather than reaching for the same stack every time. JOPAD’s frontend is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript; Jason is React and TypeScript.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The engineering degree</h2>
      <p>
        Alongside all of this I completed a B.Eng. in Civil and Environmental Engineering at the University of Port
        Harcourt, with the Environmental Engineering option, which included fieldwork, data analysis and technical
        report writing. The engineering side
        has <a href="/engineering">its own profile on this site</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Certification</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>{certification.name}</strong>, {certification.issuer} ({certification.detail}).
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/software/contact">Get in touch</a>
        <a class="btn btn--quiet" href={site.cv.software} download>Download CV (PDF)</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Profile>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .about-head {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-m);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    font-weight: 800;
    max-width: 16em;
  }

  .about-photo {
    max-width: 24rem;
  }

  .about-photo :global(img) {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 30%;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .about-text h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-top: 2.5em;
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    margin-top: 2em;
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.5fr);
      column-gap: var(--space-3xl);
    }
    .about-head {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
    .about-photo {
      position: sticky;
      top: 8rem;
      align-self: start;
    }
  }
</style>
